# Sigma REST API credentials.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. .env is gitignored.
# Find these in Sigma: Administration -> APIs and Tokens (a.k.a. Developer Access -> API credentials).
#
# Don't want to provision a client ID/secret? `eval "$(scripts/api/browser-login.sh)"`
# signs you in through the browser instead — no admin-provisioned credential
# needed, and the only auth path Sigma's /mcp/v2 accepts. This .env/
# client_credentials path is still required for headless/CI use and is what
# Claude Code web injects automatically (no .env needed there either).

# API host (NOT the app URL). Pick the one matching your org's cloud/region.
# Reference: https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/region-warehouse-and-feature-support
# Common defaults:
#   AWS US-West (Oregon):     https://aws-api.sigmacomputing.com
#   AWS US-East (N. Virginia): https://api.us-a.aws.sigmacomputing.com
#   GCP US (Iowa):            https://api.sigmacomputing.com
SIGMA_BASE_URL=https://aws-api.sigmacomputing.com

SIGMA_CLIENT_ID=
SIGMA_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Optional overrides (uncomment to use) ---

# Path to a .env file other than <repo-root>/.env, if load-env.sh should
# read from somewhere else.
# ENV_FILE=/path/to/alternate.env

# Absolute path to a token-fetcher script other than the repo-local
# scripts/api/get-token.sh — e.g. the upstream sigma-api plugin's version.
# SIGMA_TOKEN_FETCHER=/path/to/get-token.sh

# Path to the on-disk OAuth token cache. Defaults to a per-user path under
# $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR or $TMPDIR/tmp (mode 0600, 55-min TTL). Override only if
# that default doesn't suit your environment.
# SIGMA_TOKEN_CACHE=/path/to/token-cache

# Set to 1 to skip the automatic post-POST/PUT data-layer audit
# (audit-workbook-schema.sh) that publish-workbook.sh runs by default.
# SIGMA_SKIP_AUDIT=1
